                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Grand Junction CO",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:31PM MDT until October 22 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO",
                "description": "FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern Montrose County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 330 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1231 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Heavy\nrainfall rates are occurring on already saturated ground as this\narea has received between 1 and 2 inches of rain over the last 24\nhours. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nNorwood, Sawpit, Placerville and Fall Creek.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nHighway 145 between Norwood and Sawpit is prone to rockslides and\nmudslides in heavy rain. Stay alert for rocks and debris on roads,\nand avoid driving on flooded roads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
