                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:23PM MDT until October 22 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO",
                "description": "FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthwestern Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* Until 330 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1223 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between\n1 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen over the last 24 hours. Heavy\nrainfall rates due to thunderstorms are falling over this already\nsaturated area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nArboles and Chimney Rock.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nHighway 151 from Arboles to the intersection of 160 near Chimney Rock\nis prone to rockslides and mudslides in heavy rain. Stay alert for\nrocks and debris on roads, and avoid driving on flooded roads. Find\nan alternate route.",
