                "description": "FFWSLC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Salt Lake City has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Washington County in southwestern Utah...\n\n* Until 345 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1140 AM MDT, Between 1 and 2 inches of rain have fallen across\nthe headwaters of Gould Wash from earlier thunderstorms which\ncreated a large flood wave which continues to move through\nHurricane. Additional thunderstorms forming to the south and west\nare expected to move back into this area exacerbating the flooding\nwithin the next 30 to 45 minutes. Flash flooding is ongoing.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nGould Wash through Hurricane.",
